Scott's good to have you on the Dan  Patrick show it's Ross Tucker filling in  for Dan today I guess I'm curious much  than anything Scott have you heard  anything new I mean there was new Sunday  about you know this guy that you know  shot will it was in the back have we  heard anything more about motives or  what went down I haven't heard anything  I'm curious as to whether or not somehow  you guys have more information than we  do no we really don't and you know I  think little things keep coming out here  here and there you have different  witnesses stepping forward and they're  trying to put some pieces to the puzzle  together  and you know really really when the  whole story's going to come out is is  when wills wife probably feels up to  talking about that and given everybody  an idea what what actually happened but  you know you spend the day after while  you're grieving and thinking about will  going on social media finally putting a  face to the guy that took his life going  through anger and you find yourself just  going down the path of trying to put  things together and it just got  exhausting it gets really exhausting you  try to put those pieces together but you  know over time it's gonna it's going to  come together but you know I was talking  to Jonathan Vilma yesterday and as many  things we try to piece together the end  result is it doesn't matter I mean will  will still will never be back he'll  never be back with us so we just have to  let the process play out and and try to  cope as best we can you know I think I  have a pretty good sense of the type of  player that will was what kind of person  was he you know in the meeting rooms in  the locker room behind closed doors you  know will was look was one of those guys  who as good a talent as he was on the  field and so many millions of people saw  him on TV and saw how great a football  player he was he was a million times  better person and you know for me to  know him for the last ten years and get  a play seven years with him it was truly  an honor I got to see him away from the  field  how he interacted with everybody on a  day-to-day basis and will was one of  those guys who could just who he could  sit down with anybody for any amount of  time didn't matter where you grew up  what your background was what your  beliefs were what race you were what  religion it didn't matter will will get  along with everybody and if will didn't  get along with you you really had to  look in here as to what you were doing  wrong because there was a reason why  will was voted team captain every year  he was there and he was he was our  anchor he was the guy we turn to in  tough times and he was our leader along  with Jonathan Vilma both guys we  wouldn't accomplish the things we  accomplished without Will Smith and you  know that makes it even harder when when  such a great man away from the football  field was taken when you look at what he  did in the community the things he tried  to do for youth and to have that taken  away you know it's hard and when I knew  yesterday I spent a lot of time doing  interviews and talking about will and  and my phone was blown up with requests  and the initial thing to do I thought  was you know I don't want to talk about  this I want to I want to turn my phone  off but the more I thought about it the  more I thought what better way to pay  tribute and honor a great guy like will  than to talk about what type of guy he  was outside the 91 Jersey that everybody  saw yeah I think that's really well said  it's got we certainly appreciate having  you on Scott of course played a number  of years with Will Smith in New Orleans  you know I see the sack numbers Scott  and I know he went to a Pro Bowl I don't  know why he didn't go to the Pro Bowl in  2009 or wasn't voted into it or whatever  with 13 and a half sacks but looking  back on those Super Bowl teams how  valuable was he on that 2009 Super Bowl  team how important of a piece of the  puzzle was will well I'll say this will  was one of the few holdovers in 2006  when coach paint came in and was  establishing his plan and what he wanted  and will was the perfect perfect guy I  mean he embodied everything we were  trying to get done when you talk about  we wanted tough smart selfless players  who are accountable we'll embodied all  of that and we were fortunate enough to  have our entire group of guy  who embodied that and when you talk  about a team captain and a guy who will  was not a rah-rah guy he was not a jump  around getting your face type of guy but  one will spoke everybody shut up and  listened and and we knew when will spoke  it was coming from the heart and he  meant what he said and he was a leader  by example  you know you you wouldn't find a  hard-working guy a guy I can't remember  recall a guy missing a practice and it  killed him to never be on the field if  he had anything wrong with him injury  wise and you talk about he was a pro's  Pro in the ultimate teammate and  ultimate leader and I really feel like  no matter where he would have got  drafted in the NFL he would have played  as long as he did and been a key  cornerstone to any franchise in the NFL  we're talking with Scott Shanley  longtime teammate of Will Smith here  Scott you know I feel like I should ask  you I'm always curious when guys stop  playing what are you doing now when I  was done I moved back to Dallas I played  here with the Cowboys for a couple years  we really enjoyed the area my wife and  three young kids and settled back here  and you know for a year year and a half  I took time off spent time with my young  kids coached youth football still doing  that but last fall I had an opportunity  to go back to New Orleans and talk  sports television had me come down be  being analyst for the Saints games and  and I really enjoyed it I really enjoyed  going down to Orleans every weekend and  covering a team that I loved and  watching the coaches and the players  that I played with and so I that media  door opened up last fall and I really  enjoyed it enjoy talking about football  you know it's an easy transition for a  lot of us guys who when you sit 10 years  in a meeting room and learn about the  game and when somebody asks you hey what  happened on this play and you can kind  of break it down and and you combine  that with I was covering a team I love  and we want a championship in New  Orleans it was always great going back  down there last fall so hopefully that  continues this year  well hey Scott really appreciate the  time thanks for coming aboard absolutely  thanks for having me on all right there  he is Scott Shanley talking about his  former teammate Will Smith the Dan  Patrick show weekday mornings on  audience  you
 

